t(8, 2440, """Ayuba was the son of a wealthy family in Africa, who sold African slaves to the traders of the Americas at the time when slaves were transported to the Americas. He was returning from a trading trip inside his country after handing over slaves he owned to an English trader, and on the way back to his city, highwaymen from the Mandinka tribe attacked him, shaved his hair and beard, then took him to the very port he had just returned from, to sell him to the same English trader to whom he had sold slaves two days earlier! Ayuba tried to convince the English trader that he was Ayuba, the trader who had met him two days before and sold him the slaves, but the English""")

t(9, 150, """trader refused to believe him!
Ayuba lived for a few years as an oppressed slave, then was freed and returned to his family, but despite the harsh experience of slavery he had lived, he went back to selling slaves again!

Conclusion: the distance between sincerity of belief and faith in values is the same as the distance between loving the self and worshipping it!
Man is not only the son of his experience, and formation is not only the product of experience; there is something else stronger than all hard experiences .. that thing which is stronger than a thousand experiences is - the self - .. the self, not the experience!

However much a person has seen of injustice and been seared by it, he will not necessarily uphold justice after being freed from injustice!!""")

h(9, 1280, """Ayuba and the Mandinka!""")

t(9, 1625, """In the making of the mind, the many Babylonian captivity experiences speak, across their different times, old and new; to the old experience the Children of Israel were subjected, and to the new, scattered peoples today in Asia and Africa! The making of the mind in exile does not resemble its making in the homeland, so exiles share to a certain degree similar traits in mental structure that differ from those who lived the experience of the homeland. Hence the size of the difference in vision and in looking at matters among those exiled for political reasons, such as the Palestinians, Syrians, Iraqis, Arakanese, Turkestanis, Somalis and other peoples who faced the existential challenge, the extent to which exile made their minds makes a match between their mental structure and those who did not live the same experience almost nonexistent!

From this introduction, one must understand the mental and psychological influences and the way the mind is made which shaped any person, especially if he is influential in international politics, so that we can gauge and anticipate his thoughts, leanings, orientations and vision. For the influence of unstable geography on mental structure is a very large influence, the influence of the state of oppression that accompanies the exile throughout his journey of exile is a very large psychological influence, and the influence of exile on the exile's ability to shed the convictions of the collective mind is considered great, because he was never one day part of a psychologically harmonious, homogeneous human group (a people). So he is of a different structure, and this different structure cannot be done justice by a book, let alone an article, but in brief: the world today has two rival mentalities, one of them the composite mentality of directed ideology, and the other the free one, fully independent of ideology, because it did not submit to collective inheritances nor to directed ideologization within a culturally and socially cohesive collective framework. Hence the comprehensive picture will be clearer, always and not sometimes, in the mind that exile formed from the very beginning far from the molds of stable societies, and moved it early to a state of analysis, classification and very early sifting. So the foundation upon which it was built is from the start different, as a mind, from the foundation upon which the mind influenced by the collective state was built; hence exiles have always been a state of complete liberation of the mind, and those who dwell in homelands have a share of intellectual liberation, but in degrees lower than the people of exile!

Conclusion: the true goodness of the free mental structure is in its being an element of building, not demolition, an element of security, not chaos, and in helping others realize the value of the homeland and the importance of holding on to its security, because it can see the comprehensive picture and can perceive dangers more widely.""")

h(10, 650, """The exile mentality!""")

t(10, 1225, """From the chaos of the French Revolution, when it exhausted its people and they disbelieved in it, and Napoleon appeared (only at the start of his affair) as a savior of people from the revolution itself and the chaos it produced, to a model in which people achieved stability, forgetting the slogans of revolutions, humanity reaffirms that true salvation is not in the claim of absolute freedom, because it is a wide door to chaos that in the end exhausts them, so they cry out to Allah the Exalted asking Him to save them from it after they had been enthusiastic for it. True salvation is rather in the balance of the political social contract that meets the needs of social security: food, money, a decent shelter and medicine, safety from fear and tension, and living with dignity. The American and European model met the requirements of stability for 80 years according to the standards and wishes of its peoples, but after the rise of China and Russia's return to the forefront, its structure is no longer able to face competition, because for 80 years neither China nor the Soviet Union were real competitors. And because the standards of the model of the United States and the European Union in setting the rhythm of liberal standards at the level of thought and the methodology of thought, not the economy, are standards that cannot understand the necessities of balance with the Chinese and Russian models, which have finally stood on their feet, Europe and the United States today face anew the chaos of the French Revolution and the American Revolution (the chaos of long-term results), since the structure of the American-European liberal mind is still connected to expansionist, replacement liberal thought. The United States and Europe will not adjust to coexist with the world except through the emergence of leaders among them who realize the importance of internal security as a priority above the priorities of intellectual replacement, at which the United States and Europe have failed always and at all times, because they did not understand well the truth of human thought and how it works. So all Western peoples are on the verge of a decisive historical appointment in which they will witness a tsunami-like psychological shock following the collapse of the bubble of Western superiority and the melting of the lie of the West's ability to lead the world. This will be the result of the shift of the geography of world politics against the Western compass, without the existence of an American Marshall, nor a United Nations, nor veto states, nor the advanced military base in Palestine, nor many of the things that made the world after the Second World War, which saved the concepts of Western liberalism because the United States saved Europe and Europe supported the United States, producing for us 80 years of a strong Western alliance successful in imposing its vision on the whole world. But in the coming geopolitical innovation the economic and military formation will be different, and the United States will absolutely not be in it an element of strategic or tactical support for the continent of Europe. The world's political and economic weight will move to the regions of yesterday's enemies (the Arabs), and the influences of the poles of East and West will vanish. Accordingly, balances will change so that the shape of the world looks closer to what it was 1400 years ago - a closed China and two Americas unknown to the world, with Red Indian tribes living in them (complete absence of global influence), and the return of power to the Old World only and exclusively, concentrated 90% in the Middle East and 10% in Europe, the Middle East's dominance over the world, and China, Russia, India and the two Americas turning into local states whose political and economic influence on the world is worthless.""")

h(11, 500, """The French Revolution, when it disbelieved!""")

t(11, 1050, """Tell me how many enemies you had, I will tell you who and what you are! Tell me how many pains you had, I will tell you the size of the iron that dwelt in your heart! Tell me how many sorrows you had, I will tell you the truth of the roar your soul stores up! And tell me how many tears you had, I will tell you the measure of the mercy in you! Do not speak to me of anything other than this, because without it I will not see you, nor will I know you, but I will find you no more than one of the crowds.. Nothing important! Nothing distinguished! Nothing of great value worth stopping at in the battle of life!""")

h(11, 1950, """Tell me how many enemies you had!""")

t(11, 2300, """Whoever grasps the meaning, his structure becomes straight .. your structure's root is achieving certainty in Allah's Most Beautiful Names and Attributes; whoever achieves it, his destinies revolve around whichever of the Names, and he sees results before they happen, and what does not go straight for people goes straight for him, since they are tossing about on the bridge of this world in fear of tomorrow .. I am not speaking of taking the means; I am speaking of the panic that strikes people when means become scarce and are cut off!""")

